      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The best time to replace a roof in Utah is late spring through early fall (specifically between May and October), when mild temperatures and stable weather allow asphalt shingles to properly seal.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "late spring through early fall"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Seasonal Breakdown for Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Late Spring (May\u2013June):",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Rising temperatures help heat-activated shingle adhesive bond and seal\n."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Weather can sometimes bring sudden spring rain showers, but crews can work efficiently during dry windows."
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Summer (July\u2013August):",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Offers steady, dry working conditions\n\n."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Note: Peak summer heat in Utah can make asphalt shingles overly soft and vulnerable to scuffing or granule loss if workers walk on them."
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Fall (September\u2013November):",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Widely considered the gold standard because crisp, dry air and comfortable temperatures prevent material damage and help sealants cure\n."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Drawback: This is peak contractor season, meaning schedules fill up fast and you must book well in advance before early winter snowstorms arrive."
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Winter (December\u2013February):",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Generally the worst time due to snow, ice, and freezing temperatures that make shingles brittle and prone to cracking during installation\n. Only recommended for emergency repairs or leaks."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          6,
          7,
          8
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Planning Tips"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Book early: If aiming for fall or late spring, contact local contractors months ahead of time to secure your preferred window."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Don't wait on leaks:\nIf your roof is actively leaking, the best time to replace it is immediately, regardless of the season."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          9
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you want to plan your project, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What is your current roof (asphalt, metal, tile)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Is your roof currently leaking or damaged, or are you doing routine replacement?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can give you a better idea of what to expect for timelines and prep."
      }
